index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0097787bf3cfe729a914cd637a52f19e97144c49
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/08-independent-semantic-classification.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+FROZEN SOURCE COMMANDS
+nl -ba /reference/k-proof/verification.k
+nl -ba /reference/k-proof/solution.py
+nl -ba /reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/str.k | sed -n '1,22p'
+nl -ba /reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/methods.k | sed -n '9,16p;111,138p'
+nl -ba /reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k | sed -n '139,145p'
+nl -ba /reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/controls.k | sed -n '62,75p'
+
+RELEVANT EXACT SOURCE RESULTS
+verification.k:8 declares digitSumIS(IntSeq) [function, total].
+verification.k:10 is `rule digitSumIS(.IntSeq) => 0`.
+verification.k:11-16 structurally defines the iCons case as the current code
+when isUpperC(C) and notBool isLowerC(C), otherwise zero, plus digitSumIS(REST).
+solution.py:1-7 initializes total to zero, iterates `for char in s`, adds
+`ord(char)` exactly when `char.isupper()`, and returns total.
+str.k:8-10 maps string iteration on .IntSeq to done and iCons(C,R) to the
+one-character string str(iCons(C,.IntSeq)) with remainder str(R).
+methods.k:13 defines one-character isupper through
+`hasUpper(CS) andBool notBool hasLower(CS)`; lines 112-130 define isUpperC as
+65 <= C <= 90, isLowerC as 97 <= C <= 122, and hasUpper/hasLower as structural
+folds with false empty cases.
+builtins.k:143 maps ord on str(iCons(C,.IntSeq)) to C.
+controls.k:69-74 executes For through #loop/#iterNext and binds each yielded
+value before executing the body and recurring on the iterator remainder.
+
+INDEPENDENT UNIVERSAL REDUCTION
+For arbitrary integer C, the supplied iterator yields the singleton string
+containing C. On that singleton, hasUpper reduces to isUpperC(C) and hasLower
+reduces to isLowerC(C). Thus the operational branch condition is syntactically
+the same `isUpperC(C) andBool notBool isLowerC(C)` used by the recurrence; on
+the true branch ord returns the same C. Empty iteration contributes zero and
+the iCons loop executes the same step before structurally recurring on REST.
+The two verification rules therefore define the exact relevant summary rather
+than asserting a separate result property or replacing program execution.
+
+INDEPENDENT RECLASSIFICATION
+rule-e470dad5...1108c4: DEFINITION (empty constructor equation).
+rule-b3786e0b...56060: DEFINITION (nonempty structural recurrence).
+OPERATIONAL_RULE set: empty.
+PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA set: empty.
+DOMAIN_LEMMA set: empty.
+simplification-rule set: empty.
+
+ADVERSARIAL/COUNTERFACTUAL COMMAND RESULT
+COMMAND
+python /audit-output/evidence/scripts/boundary_counterfactuals.py
+
+RESULT
+code operational summary equal const0 identity lt90 lowercase
+-100 0 0 True True False True True
+0 0 0 True True True True True
+64 0 0 True True False True True
+65 65 65 True False True True False
+66 66 66 True False True True False
+89 89 89 True False True True False
+90 90 90 True False True False False
+91 0 0 True True False True True
+96 0 0 True True False True True
+97 0 0 True True False True False
